the rocky Atlantic coast of Lanzarote  Island a barren volcanic landscape and  house is painted in traditional white if  you head inland you'll find the village  of los vias and the home of Yahoo and  Oda fantasy Leon hello  welcome come on in Yaya who's Spanish  and Oda who's German met in Lanza rota  30 years ago today they rent out country  homes but this one is special it's built  largely underground this is what we call  an aji Bay an old cistern we turned it  into a small country home for centuries  the villagers stored rainwater here now  it's been turned into a holiday home  they discovered the cistern by chance  it's right next to their main house we  couldn't see how big it was  so we crawled through a hole in the  ceiling we saw that the place was half  full of water I said to my wife this is  great maybe we could build a small home  here and that's exactly what we did the  couple have divided the cistern into two  levels downstairs for living and  upstairs for sleeping they've tried to  keep the cistern pretty much as it was  we decided right away that we wouldn't  even touch the walls all we did was seal  the cracks and the result is something  that resembles a painting by a really  good artist it's wonderful don't you  think  the home is decorated with works by  local artists Yaya was born in lancer  rota and he's proud of his heritage this  dragon sculpture was created by Xavier  Ibanez the kitchen and bathroom are  located in the above-ground unit yo-yo  and Oda wanted to make sure that the  layout of this part of the house  complemented the style of the cistern  unit of course the cistern is very dark  and we decided that we wanted to provide  a contrast to that so we decided to  bring in as much light as possible  that's why there's so much glass outside  there's a small garden and a stately  palm tree in fact if it hadn't been for  the tree yeah you might not have  discovered the location at all it came  about while he was out taking photos one  day with a friend here's one of the  houses that we photographed back then  this is lost bias here you can see a  camel that's been chained to that palm  tree that wick the cistern is right next  to it but all that's left of this scene  today is the camels chains  morado El Camino  Oh des and Yaya Fanta stellen now rent  out the cistern it's a unique place to  stay in a secluded area of Lanzarote
 

